---
import Layout from '../layouts/WorkspaceLayout.astro'
const firstPrompt = 'Use Veqtor Workspace to open the Word file at [paste the file location here]. Add a comment saying "Reviewed with Veqtor Workspace." Attach it to the first paragraph with text. Keep the document text unchanged. Save the result as a new file in the same folder, then tell me where it is.'
const launchCommand = 'uv run --project /absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace veqtor-workspace --author "Your Name"'
const launchArguments = 'run\n--project\n/absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace\nveqtor-workspace\n--author\nYour Name'
---
<Layout canonicalPath="/setup" title="Get started — Veqtor Workspace" description="Connect Veqtor Workspace to Claude Desktop or ChatGPT Desktop on your Mac. Try a small edit on a copy of a Word document.">
  <div class="shell setup-heading"><p class="concept-kicker">Installation</p><h1>Start with your AI assistant.</h1><p class="section-intro">Connect Veqtor on your Mac, then try one small change on a copy of a Word file.</p></div>
  <div class="shell setup-container" data-tabs>
    <div class="example-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose your assistant"><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-claude" aria-controls="panel-claude" aria-selected="true">Claude Desktop</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-chatgpt" aria-controls="panel-chatgpt" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">ChatGPT Desktop</button></div>
    <aside class="preview-notice"><strong>Download availability</strong><span>A public Workspace installer is not available yet. If you received a preview package, use the instructions below. For the earlier product, see <a href="/veqtor-mcp">Veqtor MCP 0.5</a>.</span></aside>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-claude" aria-labelledby="tab-claude">
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Get the Mac extension</h2><p>You’ll need <a href="https://claude.com/download">Claude Desktop</a> installed and signed in. The Workspace extension will be available here when the release is ready.</p><button class="concept-button" type="button" disabled>Mac installer · Coming soon</button><p class="example-note">If you already received a preview extension, use that file for the next step.</p></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Open it in Claude Desktop</h2><p>Install the extension, enter the name you want used for new tracked changes and comments, and enable Veqtor Workspace. The first start may download the required runtime and libraries.</p><p>Open a new chat and ask Claude whether it can see the Veqtor Workspace tools.</p></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Point to a saved copy</h2><p>Make a copy of a Word file with sample text. Save and close it in Word. In Finder, select the copy and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location.</p><p>Paste that location into the request below. Veqtor uses the files you identify in your request.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-chatgpt" aria-labelledby="tab-chatgpt" hidden>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Prepare the desktop app</h2><p>Use ChatGPT Desktop on your Mac with local work enabled. The current Workspace preview needs a manual connection, the Workspace source folder and <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv</a>.</p><p class="example-note">Use the source folder supplied with your preview and keep it in a stable location. This setup is for local chats in the desktop app.</p></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Connect Veqtor in Settings</h2><p>Open Settings → MCP servers → Add server. Name it “Veqtor Workspace”, choose STDIO, and enter the connection settings below. Save, then restart the connection.</p><details class="setup-details"><summary>Show connection settings</summary><p>Set the command to <code>uv</code>. Add the following arguments, one per entry. Replace the folder location and “Your Name” with your own.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Arguments · one per line</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-arguments">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-arguments">{launchArguments}</pre></div><p>If the app cannot find uv, use its full location as the command. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp?surface=cli">OpenAI’s connection instructions</a> for the current setup options.</p></details><details class="setup-details"><summary>Using Codex CLI or the IDE extension?</summary><p>The local server also works with Codex. Add it using the same command and arguments:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Local launch command</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-command">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-command">{launchCommand}</pre></div></details></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Start with a copy of a document</h2><p>Make a copy of a Word file with sample text. Save and close it. In Finder, select the copy and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location.</p><p>Start a new chat, check that Veqtor Workspace is connected, and paste the file location into your request.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <section class="setup-step"><span>4</span><div><h2>Add your first comment</h2><p>Replace the bracketed text with the file’s location. This request adds one comment and saves a new file.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Your first request</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="first-prompt">Copy request</button></div><blockquote id="first-prompt">{firstPrompt}</blockquote></div><p>Open the result in Word and check the comment and the document. For your next text edit, ask for tracked changes if you want to review each change.</p></div></section>
    <div class="setup-trouble"><h3>Before your first task</h3><div class="questions"><details><summary>Can I keep editing in Word while the assistant works?</summary><p>Save first, and avoid editing the same file while the assistant saves it. Veqtor cannot read unsaved Word changes. If it updates a file that is still open in Word, reopen that file before continuing your manual edits.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to write code?</summary><p>You describe the document task in normal language. Claude Desktop uses an extension; the current ChatGPT Desktop setup requires a manual local connection. The document work itself does not require you to write code.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use confidential documents?</summary><p>Veqtor runs locally, but document content returned to the assistant becomes part of your AI conversation. Use documents only when processing them with your chosen AI service is permitted. Start with sample text.</p></details></div></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
